tive refractive outcome: IOL Master versus ultrasound</article-title><source>Ophthalmologica</source><year>2007</year><volume>221</volume><fpage>384</fpage><lpage>387</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17947824</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B21"><label>21</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chylack</surname><given-names>LT</given-names></name><name><surname>Wolfe</surname><given-names>JK</given-names></name><name><surname>Singer</surname><given-names>DM</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><collab>The Longitudinal Study of Cataract Study Group</collab><article-title>The lens opacities classification system III</article-title><source>Arch Ophthalmol</source><year>1993</year><volume>111</volume><fpage>831</fpage><lpage>836</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8512486</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B22"><label>22</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Findl</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Drexler</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Menapace</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Improved prediction of intraocular lens power using partial coherence interferometry</article-title><source>J Cataract Refract Surg</source><year>2001</year><volume>27</volume><fpage>861</fpage><lpage>867</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11408132</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B23"><label>23</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Eleftheriadis</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>IOL Master biometry: refractive results of 100 consecutive cases</article-title><source>Br J Ophthalmol</source><year>2003</year><volume>87</volume><fpage>960</fpage><lpage>963</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12881334</pub-id></element-citation></re