 signal-to-noise ratio (SNR) on refractive predictability</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="kjo-23-6-i003"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p><sup>*</sup>ANOVA; <sup>&#x02020;</sup>UCVA=uncorrected visual acuity; <sup>&#x02021;</sup>BCVA=best corrected visual acuity.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T4" position="float"><label>Table 4</label><caption><p>Effect of preoperative visual acuity on the signal-to-noise ratio (SNR) and refractive predictability</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="kjo-23-6-i004"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p><sup>*</sup>Grouping according to decimal VA scale; <sup>&#x02020;</sup>ANOVA; <sup>&#x02021;</sup>UCVA=uncorrected visual acuity; <sup>&#x000a7;</sup>BCVA=best corrected visual acuity.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T5" position="float"><label>Table 5</label><caption><p>Effect of PSC on preoperative visual acuity, the signal-to-noise ratio (SNR), and refractive predictability</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="kjo-23-6-i005"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p><sup>*</sup>Grading according to the LOC system III; <sup>&#x02020;</sup>Kruskal-Wallis test; <sup>&#x02021;</sup>UCVA=uncorrected visual acuity; <sup>&#x000a7;</sup>BCVA: best corrected visual acuity.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T6" position="float"><label>Table 6</label><caption><p>Effect of preoperative refraction on preoperative visual acuity, the signal-to-noise ratio (SNR), and refractive predictability</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="kjo-23-6-i006"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p><sup>*</sup>SE=spherical equivalent; <sup>&#x02020;</sup>Kruskal-Wallis test; <sup>&#x02021;</sup>UCVA=uncorrected visual acuity.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T7" position="float"><label>Table 7</label><caption><p>Effect of axial length (AL) on the SNR and refractive predictability</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="kjo-23-6-i007"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p><sup>*</sup>Kruskal-Wallis Test; <sup>&#x02020;</sup>Units in millimeters.</p></f